class:: SilenceRate
summary:: Fraction of recent RMS frames below an absolute threshold
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/DetectSilence

description::
Counts RMS frames at or below 10.pow(thresholdDB/20), divided by the observation frame count. Nonoverlapping frames and a complete-window warmup are used. Exact silence returns one after warmup. Thresholds may be arrays through multichannel expansion. Cost is linear in the frame count at each envelope update; memory is fixed at construction. This is an independent threshold-occupancy statistic.

Vanilla DetectSilence produces a state/action after sustained low level; SilenceRate describes how much of a rolling interval was quiet.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate input.

argument:: thresholdDB
Absolute RMS silence threshold, -160..0 dBFS.

argument:: windowTime
Literal window duration, 2*frameTime..10 seconds; default 0.5.

argument:: frameTime
Literal RMS frame duration, 0.001..0.1 seconds.

returns::
Fraction from zero through one.

examples::
A tone fills the sample's quieter passages, with its level and pitch set by recent silence.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var silence = SilenceRate.kr(source, -35, 0.5);
        var reply = SinOsc.ar(silence.linexp(0, 1, 180, 900), 0, silence * 0.06);
        (source * 0.2 + reply) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.6) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
Stop and release the buffer:
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

